      "description": "Display Habit Completion Icons in Calendar View\n\nAdd visual indicators to the calendar view that show an icon for each habit when it has been completed (for positive/neutral habits) or successfully avoided (for negative habits).\n\nRequirements:\n- Display the habit's category icon on calendar days where the habit was logged\n- For positive/neutral habits: show icon when habit is completed\n- For negative habits: show icon when habit is successfully avoided (not performed)\n- Support multiple habit icons per day when multiple habits are tracked\n- Ensure icons are appropriately sized and positioned within calendar day cells\n- Handle overflow gracefully when many habits are logged on a single day (consider icon size reduction, stacking, or scroll)\n- Use the existing habit category icon system (Lucide React icons)\n- Maintain visual clarity and readability at different screen sizes\n- Apply appropriate styling to distinguish completed vs. partial completion if habit has frequency targets\n- Ensure icons respect the current theme (light/dark mode) with proper contrast\n\nEdge Cases:\n- Days with many habits logged (>5 icons)\n- Habits completed multiple times per day vs. frequency target\n- Calendar view on mobile devices with limited space per day cell\n- Habits without assigned category icons\n\nDependencies:\n- Existing calendar day component structure\n- Habit category icon mapping\n- RxDB habit completion log queries by date\n- Current responsive calendar layout",
